#
# Conformance case: deception/held-projected-no-intent
# AC: intent is EVIDENCE, never ENTAILMENT, of a held/projected gap. A deception
# structure formalized as a non-Horn logic:Formula (an existential-head necessary
# condition — every deception has SOME held and SOME projected standpoint) does NOT
# lower to an evaluable rule: it is carried as flagged unsupported residue
# (SoundUnder), so the engine fabricates NEITHER a held nor a projected witness for
# a deception-typed event, and — the guardrail — it materializes NO
# gmeow:deceptiveIntentClaim. The world's only deceptive-intent fact is the one
# ASSERTED in input.nq (an attributed, defeasible assessor claim, EDB); the chase
# never derives a new one. The materialized graph therefore carries only the echoed
# EDB facts, never a fabricated held/projected witness and never a derived intent.
#
# The whole-bundle guarantee that NO rule anywhere derives gmeow:deceptiveIntentClaim
# is the standing logic:IntentNotFromDeceptionObligation (Arm A syntactic reachability
# over rule heads + Arm B finite closure), enforced over the reasoned graph by
# `make verify`; this case is its adversarial complement at the engine level.
#
# Formula: ∀e. Deception(e) → ∃h,p. (gmeow:heldStandpoint(e,h) ∧ gmeow:projectedStandpoint(e,p))

